# Phase 3 remoting transport review — 2026-09-27

- Baseline: Java RocketMQ client 5.5.1 source at `/Users/nanashi07/Projects/3rd/rocketmq`; repository plan `plan/2026/09/04-phase-03-remoting-transport.md`.
- Reviewed scan executor source: Java `scanExecutor` is `ThreadUtils.newThreadPoolExecutor(4, 10, 60s, ArrayBlockingQueue(32))`; `scanAvailableNameSrv` submits each address on every scan. Rust had unbounded JoinSet fan-out. Changed Rust to 10 probe permits and 42 total in-flight jobs per batch, rotate starting address across ticks to avoid starvation, and added `name_server_scan_batch_bounds_work_and_rotates_fairly`. Documented bounded batch and remaining rejection/overlap differences.
- Reviewed Java timeout scanning schedule in `NettyRemotingClient.start`: first `scanResponseTable` after 3s, then 1s. Changed Rust `timeout_scheduler` to the same nominal cadence and updated the inventory.
- Reviewed Java NameServer index: `initValueIndex()` initializes `new Random().nextInt(999)` and selection uses `incrementAndGet`, `Math.abs`, then modulo. Rust constructor now seeds from 0..999 and increments before modulo in the fallback selection path; inventory records the mapped initial counter and notes list/wrapper behavior still differs.
- Fixed already-expired async callback metadata to retain `Operation` phase and remote address; adjusted the corresponding callback expectation for contextual timeout.
- Executor/lifecycle comparison remains only partially mapped. Address-only channel-event callback and Tokio lifecycle/thread/polling/shutdown/drain differences are explicitly accepted by user; this is not treated as waiving queue/admission, callback ordering, task behavior, or missing feature gaps. Inventory retains `PARTIAL` rows for Java Channel/ResponseFuture surfaces, wrappers, callback/processor executor behavior and Rust-vs-Java scheduling/rejection differences.
- Acceptance evidence: P3-V01/V02/V03/U01 are represented by named automated race, connection generation, backlog/inbound, raw route/TLS/deadline/shutdown tests, but phase plan boxes remain unchecked until the parity review closes. P3-V04 is deferred to Phase 19. No Phase 3 acceptance declared.
- Validation after implementation: `cargo fmt --all --check`; `cargo test --workspace --offline` (49 remoting unit, 4 codec, 74 transport plus workspace tests); `cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets --offline -- -D warnings`; `python3 scripts/check-workspace-metadata.py`; `python3 tests/differential/compare.py --self-test`; `git diff --check` all passed. An earlier test attempt exposed a stale test expectation and the direct-expired callback path; fixed and reran successfully.
- Status: changes remain uncommitted pending full change review and Phase 3 discrepancy disposition. Phase 4 must not start.
